{"type":"thinking","text":"Now we need to understand the task. The prompt says deliver: executable four-slot shift plan, per-vehicle release slips, and handover. Explain departure charge, margin, low-efficiency handling.\n\nImportant nuance from the context and tools: There is a \"DUTY-2340\" 23:40 measured per-slot upper limit that supersedes the 21:00 capture and old building load estimates. The depot_release_check tool description says: \"R4 本班在原四格半小时、车辆窗口、20 kW 预约平移及同一冷夜工况下，23:40 DUTY-2340 的逐格实测上限已计入当班负荷，取代 21:00 采集和旧楼宇负荷推算。按适用实测窗口最大化可用充电量；工况或窗口变化须另核依据。\"\n\nThis is crucial. The original-receipt.json has run DUTY-2340 at 23:40 with limits [80,40,50,70], actual [80,40,50,50], departureKwh [126,121], withinLimits false. But the current shift-plan.json is [80,40,70,50] which is based on 21:00 cold-cycle limits [80,40,70,50]? Let's compute cold-cycle limits:\n- 00:00: (6040-6000)*60/30 = 80\n- 00:30: (6060-6040)*60/30 = 40\n- 01:00: (6095-6060)*60/30 = 70\n- 01:30: (6120-6095)*60/30 = 50\n\nSo cold-cycle limits are [80,40,70,50]. That's exactly shift-plan and the handover table. But the DUTY-2340 at 23:40 has limits [80,40,50,70] — different at slots 2 and 3 (swapped-ish: 50,70 vs 70,50). The desk note says \"DESK-21 为 21:00 同班冷夜数字站控台架的交流电表采集，线上参数按适用记录的采集时间生效。\" The tool description says 23:40 DUTY-2340's per-slot measured limits have already accounted for shift load and supersede 21:00 capture and old building load estimates. \"按适用实测窗口最大化可用充电量；工况或窗口变化须另核依据。\"\n\nSo we need to use the 23:40 DUTY-2340 limits [80,40,50,70], not the 21:00 cold-cycle [80,40,70,50]. Under the 23:40 limits, what is the maximum available charge and departure? A window slots 0-1: 80 + 40 = 120 AC over 2 slots = 60 kWh AC → battery 54 at 90% → A departure 126. B window slots 2-3: 50 + 70 = 120 AC → 54 kWh battery → B departure 130. Oh interesting! Both windows total 120 AC, same as before but distributed differently. With A at [80,40] and B at [50,70]? Wait shift-plan has B slots [70,50], but under DUTY limits, max actual is min(request, limit) = [70→min(70,50)=50, 50→min(50,70)=50]. So actual [80,40,50,50], departure A=126, B=76+0.45*(50+50)=76+45=121. So B short 9 kWh. That matches original-receipt departureKwh [126,121]. So under 23:40 applicable limits, the current plan leaves B at 121, short 9.\n\nBut we're told to maximize available charging per applicable measured window. So we should adjust shift-plan to [80,40,50,70], i.e., B gets 50 in slot 2 and 70 in slot 3. Then B departure = 76 + 0.45*(50+70) = 76+54 = 130. A stays 126. That matches the handover table's departure values but with a different distribution: A [80,40], B [50,70]. Wait handover currently has B [70,50]. But the old handover is based on 21:00 capture [80,40,70,50]. Need to revise.\n\nSo the task: update shift-plan.json to maximize charging under DUTY-2340 limits [80,40,50,70], resulting acKw [80,40,50,70]. Then compute release at 90%: A 126, margin 0; B 130, margin 0. At 85%: A = 72 + (80+40)*0.5*0.85 = 72 + 60*0.85 = 72+51 = 123 (required 126, gap 3); B = 76 + (50+70)*0.5*0.85 = 76 + 60*0.85 = 76+51 = 127 (required 130, gap 3). So at85 both HOLD (gaps 3 each). Good.\n\nBut wait, maybe we need to maximize more? \"按适用实测窗口最大化可用充电量\" — maximize available charge under applicable measured window. DUTY limits are per-slot caps. Max per window: A [80,40] = 120 AC; B [50,70] = 120 AC. That's full use. The shift-plan requested acKw might be set to the limits. But \"withinLimits\" should be true. Let's set [80,40,50,70].\n\nBut then what about the \"20 kW 平移已预约\" and building loads? The DUTY-2340 limits \"已计入当班负荷\" (already account for shift load). So we use measured limits directly. The tool description says \"23:40 DUTY-2340 的逐格实测上限已计入当班负荷，取代 21:00 采集和旧楼宇负荷推算。\" Good.\n\nNow what about model.mjs? README says submit model.mjs export plan(night, efficiency). It already exists and tests pass presumably. But the model is based on night.json building loads (cold: [40,100,50,50] then shift 20 from slot1 to slot3 → [40,80,50,70]) → caps = [80,40,70,50] at 90%. That's the 21:00 capture, not DUTY-2340. Hmm. There's tension: model.mjs is the research/model part, shift-plan/release/handover are business task. The task says \"请为河湾车队明早的冷夜班次签发现行调度工单：提交可执行的四格班表、逐车放行单和交班稿\". The README says submit model.mjs too, but that may be background. The release-format says \"排班保持现有字段、两车时窗、20 kW 已预约平移和高效工况下最大可用充电量。逐车决定以车辆离场可用净电量为准。修订 shift-plan.json、HANDOVER.md，新建 release.json。\"\n\n\"高效工况下最大可用充电量\" = max available charge under high-efficiency condition. Under DUTY limits, max is [80,40,50,70]. So update.\n\nBut wait, \"排班保持现有字段\" means keep existing fields of shift-plan: slotStart, bus, acKw, loadShiftKw, dispatchAt85. So we update acKw and dispatchAt85. What should dispatchAt85 be? It's \"85% 效率下的双车放行决定\". At 85%, both HOLD (gap 3 each). So dispatchAt85 = false (meaning don't dispatch at 85). The field is a boolean representing whether to dispatch at 85%. So false.\n\nNow evidenceSha: \"evidenceSha 为依据记录所指的完整 Git SHA.\" The依据记录 is the applicable record: DUTY-2340 23:40 original-receipt.json? It has \"sha\": \"341e19e288de9f561f85fcb66a7a910ff6f3e143\". That's the full Git SHA referenced by the record. But the tool \"depot_trial\" replays \"the committed four-slot sheet at the named full Git SHA against the meter capture.\" And depot_contact asks previous shift's maintainer to check a committed sheet. depot_release_check checks committed dispatch order at a SHA.\n\nWe need to commit our changes and then use the full Git SHA of the commit as evidenceSha? Let's think. release-format: \"evidenceSha 为依据记录所指的完整 Git SHA。\" = the full Git SHA pointed to by the evidence record. The original-receipt.json has sha field 341e19... which might be the commit that contains the applicable DUTY-2340 record. But our new sheet needs to be committed, and evidenceSha should point to the record that the release is based on. Possibly the SHA of the commit where we commit the sheet? Let's investigate git repo."}
